00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:48.700
name at 5% of total capital. That way even an 8% adverse move costs the portfolio only 0.4%.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:55.700
Stop losses fixed at 7% to 10% below entry or trailing based on 14-day average true range

00:09:55.700 --> 00:10:01.500
automate exits before small losses compound. The simplified kelly criterion further

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:08.000
refines this. Position size equals win probability times payoff ratio minus loss probability divided

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:15.820
by payoff ratio. Even a conservative 0.25 times kelly on a 55% win rate strategy prevents overbedding

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:21.740
during emotional conviction moments. Correlation matters too because 3 energy names at 5% each

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:29.360
still act like a 12% sector bet if oil correlation exceeds 0.7. Portfolio drawdowns above 15%

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:36.260
historically take 18-24 months to recover. Professionals always calculate the exact dollar risk,

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:43.120
account size times 1% maximum loss before they choose position size or stop level, never the reverse.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:48.720
The biggest mistake with risk management is treating high conviction ideas as unlimited bets

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:54.500
or moving stops farther away as a position goes against you. Instead, always define your maximum

00:10:54.500 --> 00:11:00.060
portfolio loss first then let the math dictate the share count. Open your brokerage account right now

